      "body": "- [✅] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\r\n\r\n# What does this PR do ?\r\n<!-- Add a one line overview of what this PR aims to accomplish. -->\r\nI ran into an issue where gradients kept growing during the backward pass after enabling recompute. \r\nAfter debugging, I traced the root cause to `DeepepManager.token_probs` not being properly released. This caused the corresponding leaf tensor `hidden_states` (with `retain_grad()` applied) and its `hidden_states.grad` to remain unfreed. \r\nThe issue was resolved by assigning `None` to `self.token_probs` after the `combine` step.\r\n\r\n:warning: For major changes (either in lines of code or in its impact), please make sure to first share a design doc with the team. If you're unsure what's the best way to do so, contact @NVIDIA/mcore-oncall.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"289\" height=\"246\" alt=\"Clipboard_Screenshot_1780988475\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/872fc086-3861-46a1-bda2-6e0a71ba33b9\" />\r\n\r\nAfter fixed:\r\n<img width=\"284\" height=\"277\" alt=\"Clipboard_Screenshot_1780988626\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0d37524d-b78a-4897-8682-72c440ae2a80\" />\r\n\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
