            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "YangFei1990"
            },
            "body": "> LGTM — the fix correctly releases `token_indices` and `token_probs` in `_DeepepManager.combine()`, matching the existing pattern for `dispatched_indices`/`dispatched_probs`.\r\n> \r\n> **Non-blocking note:** `_HybridEPManager.combine()` (line ~1120) has a similar pattern — it stores `self.token_probs` and `self.dispatched_probs` during `setup_metadata`/`dispatch` but does not release them in `combine()`. Might be worth a follow-up to apply the same cleanup there.\r\n\r\n@yuyang66 Thanks for the PR. Could you also address the same pattern for the HybridEP combine?",
            "createdAt": "2026-06-12T16:51:53Z",
            "databaseId": 4693353018,
            "updatedAt": "2026-06-12T16:51:53Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/5227#issuecomment-4693353018"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "YangFei1990"
            },
            "body": "@yuyang66 Are you running with cuda graphs? Actually after checking the code these are registered as `cudagraph_attrs `: https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/megatron/core/transformer/moe/token_dispatcher.py#L1430, cuda graph will use them as outputs and always re-register them to the dispatcher after mlp post-process. Technically speaking deallocate is not harmful, but it would be save to keep them when partial cuda graph is enabled.",
            "createdAt": "2026-06-25T02:11:38Z",
            "databaseId": 4795219498,
            "updatedAt": "2026-06-25T02:11:38Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/5227#issuecomment-4795219498"
